== T2 watcher condition (EOQ algebra) and the escalation refinement ==
main-only cost: sqrt(2)*sqrt(c_main)*sigma*sqrt(w) | watcher cost: sqrt(2)*sqrt(c_w)*sigma*sqrt(w) + h_w
watcher pays iff   sqrt(2)*sqrt(c_main)*sigma*sqrt(w) - sqrt(2)*sqrt(c_w)*sigma*sqrt(w) - h_w > 0  i.e. sqrt(2w)*sigma*(sqrt(c_main)-sqrt(c_w)) > h_w  [verified symbolic]
with escalation fraction eps (each escalated check also wakes main):  pays iff sqrt(2)*sqrt(c_main)*sigma*sqrt(w) - h_w - sqrt(2)*sigma*sqrt(w)*sqrt(c_main*epsilon + c_w) > 0
  necessary: eps < 1 - c_w/c_main
eps=0.0: simulated cost 0.4472 vs formula sigma*sqrt(2w(c_w+eps c_main)) 0.4472; main-only 1.4142
eps=0.2: simulated cost 0.7756 vs formula sigma*sqrt(2w(c_w+eps c_main)) 0.7746; main-only 1.4142
eps=0.5: simulated cost 1.0945 vs formula sigma*sqrt(2w(c_w+eps c_main)) 1.0954; main-only 1.4142

== T3a compression threshold: N facts share a driver (rate q_g) plus own residual (q_u) ==
flat cost: sqrt(2)*N*sqrt(c)*sqrt(w)*sqrt(q_g + q_u)
nested cost (upper bound): sqrt(2)*sqrt(N)*sqrt(c_g)*sqrt(q_g)*sqrt(w) + sqrt(2)*N*sqrt(c)*sqrt(q_u)*sqrt(w) + h
N* (c_g=c, h=0): [rho/(rho - 2*sqrt(rho + 1) + 2)]
equals (sqrt(1+rho)+1)^2/rho ? [True]
  rho=0.1: N* = 41.98   (small-rho approx 4/rho = 40.0)
  rho=0.5: N* = 9.90   (small-rho approx 4/rho = 8.0)
  rho=1: N* = 5.83   (small-rho approx 4/rho = 4.0)
  rho=4: N* = 2.62   (small-rho approx 4/rho = 1.0)
  rho=10: N* = 1.86   (small-rho approx 4/rho = 0.4)

