== T7a scale-free banding: mean penalty for log-uniform items in a band of log-width D (geometric band, centered) ==
mean penalty = -(D - 2*sinh(D/2))/D
at D=ln2: 1 + penalty = sqrt(2)/(2*log(2)) = 1.0201394465967895  (Roundy 1985 power-of-two bound 1/(sqrt2 ln2) = 1.0201)
worst-case at band edge D=ln2: 0.06066017177982129  (Roundy fixed-base bound ~6%)

== T7b optimal number of levels K for a log-span L of natural intervals, base cost C, per-level upkeep h ==
small-band approx: K* = 18**(1/3)*C**(1/3)*L**(2/3)/(6*h**(1/3))
  L=ln(1000) C=100 h=0.5: K* exact 9, approx 9.26; level ratio e^(L/K*) = 2.15
  L=ln(100000) C=100 h=0.5: K* exact 13, approx 13.02; level ratio e^(L/K*) = 2.42

== T7c coarse-graining: unit of size n, check cost ~ n^gamma, stakes ~ n^delta, aggregate drift variance ~ n^(2H) ==
T*(n) = sqrt(2)*sqrt(c0)*n**(-H - delta/2 + gamma/2)/(s0*sqrt(w0))  => log-log slope -H - delta/2 + gamma/2
  var of sum of 8 RWs at t=50 / (8*50): 0.989

